<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47222" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">symphōnĭăcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμφωνιακός.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to concerts</i> or <i>to
				music</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pueri,</span>”
				i. e. <i>singingboys</i>, <i>choristers</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mil. 21, 55</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Div. in Caecil. 17, 55</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 5, 25, § 64</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 73</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Herba, <i>a plant</i>, <i>called
			also</i> hyoscyamos, <i>henbane</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Pall. 3, 12</span></i>. 8;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. 3, 68</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 4</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
